{
  "record": "glm-spread-vs-sampling-noise-v1",
  "date": "2026-11-21",
  "question": "Is the across-seed spread a seed-role effect, or the sampling noise of a held-out AUROC at this test-set size and class balance?",
  "prediction": {
    "registered_before_any_number": true,
    "benchmark": "a held-out AUROC's null sampling sd is sqrt((n1+n2+1)/(12*n1*n2)); at the committed geometry that is about 0.0409 and the grid's observed across-seed sd is 0.0410",
    "if_the_benchmark_fits_the_floor": "the across-seed spread is test-set sampling noise, no seed role carries it, and the only lever on the error bar is test-set size. A (B+D+E)/A ratio near 3 is then what a noise-dominated score gives, NOT role cancellation.",
    "if_A2_replicates_across_offsets": "stream sharing really does suppress the reported spread, the runner's error bars are biased LOW, and a seed-role split becomes a correctness fix -- the opposite recommendation",
    "if_A2_does_not_replicate": "the single resolvable seed-role result was an artifact of one arbitrary offset choice and must be withdrawn"
  },
