  "honest_limits": [
    "The Mann-Whitney benchmark is the null variance for exchangeable classes. It applies exactly to the perfect-generator floor, whose true AUROC is 0.5 by construction, and only approximately to the Markov null, whose true AUROC is above 0.5.",
    "It also assumes the discriminator's score is a fixed function. Here the classifier is refitted per split, which adds variance the formula does not model, so the benchmark is a LOWER bound on what to expect rather than an exact prediction.",
    "The expected test-half class counts are used; the actual split is random, so n1 and n2 vary slightly between replicates.",
    "The swept floor spreads come from 10 seeds each, where the sd of an sd estimate is roughly 24% of its value. Ratios inside about 0.76-1.24 are not mismatches, and that band is wide.",
    "Arm A2 is tested at five offset pairs; offsets are an unbounded space and five is not a proof that none behaves differently.",
    "Measured on the MARKOV candidate at one geometry, one organism, one null."
  ],
